const e={"guide-what-you-get":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>What it is</th><th>Depends on</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>@wf-controls/data</code></td><td>In-memory ADO.NET: <code>DataSet</code>, <code>DataTable</code>, <code>DataView</code>, <code>DataRow</code>, <code>DataColumn</code>, <code>DataRelation</code>. No DOM, no dependencies.</td><td>nothing</td></tr><tr><td><code>@wf-controls/core</code></td><td>Headless controllers: <code>GridView</code>, <code>DataGrid</code>, <code>Repeater</code>, <code>DataList</code>, validators, <code>Login*</code> security controls, <code>Menu</code>, <code>TreeView</code>, <code>SiteMapPath</code>, <code>Calendar</code>, <code>Xml</code>, <code>AdRotator</code>, behaviors, data sources. Re-exports <code>@wf-controls/data</code>.</td><td><code>@wf-controls/data</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>@wf-controls/react</code></td><td>React components that render the core controllers.</td><td><code>@wf-controls/core</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>@wf-controls/angular</code></td><td>Angular standalone components (<code>wf-grid-view</code>, <code>wf-repeater</code>).</td><td><code>@wf-controls/core</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The core is <strong>headless</strong>: it contains state, rules and events, never markup. You render it with React, Angular, or plain DOM code (the tutorial does the last one). There is no jQuery package yet, despite what older notes say.</p>
`,"which-package-do-i-import-from":`<h3 id="which-package-do-i-import-from">Which package do I import from?<a class="anchor" href="#which-package-do-i-import-from" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<ul><li>Building with <strong>plain TypeScript / DOM</strong>: <code>@wf-controls/core</code> (it already re-exports every data class) plus your own rendering.</li><li>Building with <strong>React</strong> or <strong>Angular</strong>: the adapter package for the UI, and <code>@wf-controls/core</code> for the controllers and data classes you pass to it.</li><li>Only need <strong>tables in memory</strong> (no controls): <code>@wf-controls/data</code>.</li></ul>
<blockquote class="note"><p><strong>Note:</strong> keep exactly <strong>one copy</strong> of <code>@wf-controls/data</code> installed. The controllers use <code>instanceof DataTable</code> / <code>DataView</code>, which fails if two copies of the package end up in your bundle. In an npm workspace this is automatic.</p></blockquote>
<hr>
`},"guide-install-and-build":{overview:`<p>This repository is an npm workspace. From the repo root:</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">powershell</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-powershell"><span class="tok-f">npm</span> install            <span class="tok-c"># link all workspaces</span>
<span class="tok-f">npm</span> run build          <span class="tok-c"># data -&gt; core -&gt; react -&gt; angular</span>
<span class="tok-f">npm</span> test               <span class="tok-c"># data tests, then core tests (node --test)</span>
<span class="tok-f">npm</span> run demo           <span class="tok-c"># run the 14 CLI demos</span></code></pre></div>
<p>To use the packages from another workspace project, depend on them by version (<code>&quot;@wf-controls/core&quot;: &quot;1.0.0&quot;</code>) and import normally:</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>, <span class="tok-t">DataTable</span>, <span class="tok-t">DataView</span>, <span class="tok-t">LoginController</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/core&quot;</span>;</code></pre></div>
<p>Build individual packages with <code>npm run build:data</code>, <code>build:core</code>, <code>build:react</code>, <code>build:angular</code>. The packages are ES modules; TypeScript users should enable <code>strict</code>. The library itself is written with <code>exactOptionalPropertyTypes</code> and <code>noUncheckedIndexedAccess</code>, so optional options are typed <code>T | undefined</code>.</p>
<hr>
`},"guide-core-concepts":{"controllers-options-and-state":`<h3 id="31-controllers-options-and-state">3.1 Controllers, options and state<a class="anchor" href="#31-controllers-options-and-state" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<p>Every control is a <strong>controller class</strong> you construct with an options object. Options become public properties or <code>options.*</code> fields, and the controller exposes methods that change state and events that report it.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">const</span> grid = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>&lt;<span class="tok-t">Employee</span>&gt;({
  id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;gvEmployees&quot;</span>,
  dataKeyField: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>,
  columns: [<span class="tok-c">/* ... */</span>],
  allowPaging: <span class="tok-k">true</span>,
  pageSize: <span class="tok-n">6</span>,
});
<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">dataBind</span>(rows);
grid.visibleRows;   <span class="tok-c">// what to render now</span>
grid.pageCount;     <span class="tok-c">// derived state</span></code></pre></div>
<p>Rendering is your job (or an adapter's). A render function typically reads <code>visibleRows</code>, <code>options.editIndex</code>, <code>currentSort</code>, and so on, and repaints whenever <code>stateChanged</code> fires.</p>
`,"events-subscribe-emit-cancel":`<h3 id="32-events-subscribe-emit-cancel">3.2 Events: <code>subscribe</code>, <code>emit</code>, cancel<a class="anchor" href="#32-events-subscribe-emit-cancel" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<p>Events are <code>EventDispatcher</code> instances. <code>subscribe(handler)</code> returns a function that unsubscribes. Handlers receive <code>(sender, args)</code> and <strong>may be async</strong>: the controller awaits each handler, in subscription order, before it continues.</p>
<p>Events that precede a change (<code>rowDeleting</code>, <code>rowUpdating</code>, <code>pageIndexChanging</code>, <code>loggingIn</code>, ...) have args that extend <code>CancelEventArgs</code>. Set <code>e.cancel = true</code> to stop the operation. All handlers still run; the controller checks the flag after the last one.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">const</span> unsubscribeA = grid.rowDeleting.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>(<span class="tok-k">async</span> (_g, e) =&gt; {
  console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;A sees row&quot;</span>, e.rowIndex);
  <span class="tok-k">await</span> <span class="tok-t">Promise</span>.<span class="tok-f">resolve</span>();                 <span class="tok-c">// async work is awaited</span>
});
grid.rowDeleting.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>((_g, e) =&gt; {
  console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;B cancels&quot;</span>);
  e.cancel = <span class="tok-k">true</span>;
});
console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;deleted:&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">deleteRow</span>(<span class="tok-n">0</span>), <span class="tok-s">&quot;| rows left:&quot;</span>, grid.totalRecords);
<span class="tok-c">// A sees row 0</span>
<span class="tok-c">// B cancels</span>
<span class="tok-c">// deleted: false | rows left: 2</span>
<span class="tok-f">unsubscribeA</span>();</code></pre></div>
<blockquote class="note"><p><strong>Note:</strong> because handlers are awaited, a <code>rowDeleting</code> handler can <code>await</code> a confirmation dialog and cancel when the user answers no. The tutorial does exactly that.</p></blockquote>
`,"the-command-pattern":`<h3 id="33-the-command-pattern">3.3 The command pattern<a class="anchor" href="#33-the-command-pattern" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<p>Row-oriented controls route string commands, as <code>CommandName</code> / <code>CommandArgument</code> do in Web Forms. <code>executeCommand(rowIndex, &quot;Edit&quot; | &quot;Delete&quot; | &quot;Select&quot; | &quot;Cancel&quot;, arg?)</code> raises <code>rowCommand</code>, then performs the matching operation (which raises its own cancellable events). Wire your buttons to <code>executeCommand</code> and keep behavior in event handlers.</p>
`,"no-postbacks":`<h3 id="34-no-postbacks">3.4 No postbacks<a class="anchor" href="#34-no-postbacks" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Web Forms</th><th>Here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Page_Load</code>, <code>!IsPostBack</code></td><td>Your app start-up code. Run it once.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ViewState</code></td><td>State lives in the controller objects. Persist it yourself (<code>localStorage</code>, REST) if you need to.</td></tr><tr><td>Postback event handlers</td><td>Events on the controller (<code>grid.rowUpdating.subscribe(...)</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>DataBind()</code></td><td><code>await controller.dataBind(data?)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Session[...]</code></td><td><code>SessionParameter</code> for data sources, or your own storage.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Page.IsValid</code>, <code>ValidationGroup</code></td><td><code>ValidatorManager.validate(group)</code> and the same group names.</td></tr><tr><td>Membership / <code>FormsAuthentication</code></td><td><code>IMembershipProvider</code>, <code>SecurityManager</code>, <code>LoginController</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<hr>
`},"guide-the-data-library":{overview:`<p><code>@wf-controls/data</code> mirrors the parts of ADO.NET you use day to day. Complete reference: <a href="#/api/data-library/ado-net-to-typescript-mapping">undefined API</a>.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">DataTable</span>, <span class="tok-t">DataColumn</span>, <span class="tok-t">DataView</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/data&quot;</span>;

<span class="tok-k">const</span> people = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">DataTable</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;People&quot;</span>);
people.columns.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(<span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">DataColumn</span>({ columnName: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, dataType: <span class="tok-s">&quot;number&quot;</span>, autoIncrement: <span class="tok-k">true</span> }));
people.columns.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;name&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;string&quot;</span>);
people.columns.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;age&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;number&quot;</span>);
people.primaryKey = [people.columns.<span class="tok-k">get</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>)!];

people.rows.<span class="tok-f">add</span>({ name: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Ada&quot;</span>, age: <span class="tok-n">36</span> });
people.rows.<span class="tok-f">add</span>({ name: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Alan&quot;</span>, age: <span class="tok-n">41</span> });
people.rows.<span class="tok-f">add</span>({ name: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Grace&quot;</span>, age: <span class="tok-n">85</span> });
<span class="tok-c">// rows: 3 | states: Added,Added,Added</span>

people.<span class="tok-f">acceptChanges</span>();                       <span class="tok-c">// everything becomes Unchanged</span>
people.<span class="tok-f">find</span>(<span class="tok-n">2</span>)!.<span class="tok-f">setItem</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;age&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-n">42</span>);           <span class="tok-c">// find() uses primaryKey</span>
<span class="tok-c">// Alan state: Modified | original age: 41 | current age: 42</span>
people.<span class="tok-f">find</span>(<span class="tok-n">3</span>)!.<span class="tok-k">delete</span>();                     <span class="tok-c">// marked Deleted, not removed yet</span>
<span class="tok-c">// count after delete: 2 | total incl. deleted: 3</span>

<span class="tok-k">const</span> view = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">DataView</span>(people);
view.rowFilter = <span class="tok-s">&quot;age &gt; 40&quot;</span>;                  <span class="tok-c">// or a predicate: (row) =&gt; row.item(&quot;age&quot;) &gt; 40</span>
view.sort = <span class="tok-s">&quot;age DESC&quot;</span>;
console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(view.<span class="tok-f">toObjects</span>());                <span class="tok-c">// [{ id: 2, name: &quot;Alan&quot;, age: 42 }]  (Grace is Deleted)</span>

people.<span class="tok-f">acceptChanges</span>();                       <span class="tok-c">// deleted rows are physically removed</span>
<span class="tok-c">// after acceptChanges rows: 2 Unchanged,Unchanged</span></code></pre></div>
<p>Points worth remembering:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Row states</strong> (<code>Added</code>, <code>Modified</code>, <code>Deleted</code>, <code>Unchanged</code>, <code>Detached</code>) and <strong>versions</strong> (<code>Current</code>, <code>Original</code>, <code>Proposed</code>) behave like ADO.NET. <code>acceptChanges()</code> / <code>rejectChanges()</code> exist on the row, the table and the set.</li><li><code>row.delete()</code> only marks a row. Rows leave the table when you call <code>acceptChanges()</code>.</li><li>Filters are a small expression language (<code>field op literal</code>, joined by <code>AND</code> / <code>OR</code>). For anything richer pass a <strong>predicate function</strong> to <code>rowFilter</code> or <code>table.select</code>.</li><li>Several constraints are only declarative: <code>unique</code> and <code>primaryKey</code> are <strong>not enforced</strong>, and the auto-increment counter is consumed even by discarded rows. See <a href="#/api/guides/issues-data-library-wf-controls-data/overview/2-data-library-wf-controlsdata">Known issues</a>.</li></ul>
`,"master-detail-with-dataset-and-datarelation":`<h3 id="41-master--detail-with-dataset-and-datarelation">4.1 Master / detail with <code>DataSet</code> and <code>DataRelation</code><a class="anchor" href="#41-master--detail-with-dataset-and-datarelation" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">DataSet</span>, <span class="tok-t">DataTable</span>, <span class="tok-t">DataRelation</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/data&quot;</span>;

<span class="tok-k">const</span> ds = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">DataSet</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;Shop&quot;</span>);
<span class="tok-k">const</span> customers = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">DataTable</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;Customers&quot;</span>);
customers.columns.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;number&quot;</span>); customers.columns.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;name&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;string&quot;</span>);
<span class="tok-k">const</span> orders = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">DataTable</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;Orders&quot;</span>);
orders.columns.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;number&quot;</span>); orders.columns.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;customerId&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;number&quot;</span>); orders.columns.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;total&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;number&quot;</span>);
ds.tables.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(customers); ds.tables.<span class="tok-f">add</span>(orders);

customers.rows.<span class="tok-f">add</span>({ id: <span class="tok-n">1</span>, name: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Contoso&quot;</span> }); customers.rows.<span class="tok-f">add</span>({ id: <span class="tok-n">2</span>, name: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Fabrikam&quot;</span> });
orders.rows.<span class="tok-f">add</span>({ id: <span class="tok-n">10</span>, customerId: <span class="tok-n">1</span>, total: <span class="tok-n">99</span> });
orders.rows.<span class="tok-f">add</span>({ id: <span class="tok-n">11</span>, customerId: <span class="tok-n">1</span>, total: <span class="tok-n">25</span> });
orders.rows.<span class="tok-f">add</span>({ id: <span class="tok-n">12</span>, customerId: <span class="tok-n">2</span>, total: <span class="tok-n">5</span> });

<span class="tok-c">// DataRelation(name, parentTable, childTable, parentColumn(s), childColumn(s)): columns are given by NAME.</span>
<span class="tok-k">const</span> rel = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">DataRelation</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;CustomerOrders&quot;</span>, customers, orders, <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;customerId&quot;</span>);
ds.relations.<span class="tok-f">push</span>(rel);                        <span class="tok-c">// relations is a plain array</span>

<span class="tok-k">const</span> contoso = customers.<span class="tok-f">select</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;id = 1&quot;</span>)[<span class="tok-n">0</span>]!;
console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(rel.<span class="tok-f">getChildRows</span>(contoso).<span class="tok-f">map</span>((r) =&gt; r.<span class="tok-f">item</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;total&quot;</span>)));   <span class="tok-c">// [ 99, 25 ]</span></code></pre></div>
<hr>
`},"guide-binding-data-to-controls":{overview:`<p><code>GridViewController</code> and <code>RepeaterController</code> accept an <strong>array</strong>, a <strong><code>DataView</code></strong> or a <strong>data source control</strong> (<code>SqlDataSource</code>, <code>ObjectDataSource</code>, ...). <code>DataGridController</code> and <code>DataListController</code> are more limited; check <a href="#/api/data-controls/asp-net-to-typescript-mapping">Data controls</a> for the exact matrix.</p>
<blockquote class="warn"><p><strong>Warning:</strong> bind a <strong><code>DataView</code></strong> (<code>new DataView(table)</code>), not the <code>DataTable</code> itself, to a <code>GridViewController</code>. A <code>DataTable</code> has a <code>select</code> method, so the controller mistakes it for a data source control and <code>sort()</code>, <code>updateRow()</code> and <code>deleteRow()</code> then misbehave or throw.</p></blockquote>
<blockquote class="warn"><p><strong>Warning:</strong> <code>dataBind()</code> <strong>copies</strong> the rows (<code>row.toObject()</code>). Editing or deleting through the grid changes that copy, not your <code>DataTable</code>. Persist in <code>rowUpdating</code> / <code>rowDeleting</code> (or in your own method) and call <code>dataBind()</code> again to resynchronise.</p></blockquote>
<p>The standard CRUD pattern, in short:</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">const</span> view = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">DataView</span>(table);
<span class="tok-k">const</span> grid = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>&lt;<span class="tok-t">Employee</span>&gt;({ id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;gv&quot;</span>, dataKeyField: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, columns, dataSource: view, allowPaging: <span class="tok-k">true</span>, pageSize: <span class="tok-n">6</span> });

grid.rowUpdating.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>((_g, e) =&gt; {
  <span class="tok-k">try</span> { store.<span class="tok-f">update</span>(e.dataItem.id, { ...e.dataItem, ...e.values }); }   <span class="tok-c">// write to the DataTable</span>
  <span class="tok-k">catch</span> (err) { e.cancel = <span class="tok-k">true</span>; }                                       <span class="tok-c">// refuse the edit</span>
});
grid.rowDeleting.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>(<span class="tok-k">async</span> (_g, e) =&gt; {
  <span class="tok-k">if</span> (!(<span class="tok-k">await</span> <span class="tok-f">confirmDialog</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;Delete?&quot;</span>))) { e.cancel = <span class="tok-k">true</span>; <span class="tok-k">return</span>; }
  store.<span class="tok-f">remove</span>(e.dataItem.id);
});

<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">dataBind</span>();                       <span class="tok-c">// first load</span>
<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">executeCommand</span>(<span class="tok-n">2</span>, <span class="tok-s">&quot;Edit&quot;</span>);        <span class="tok-c">// user pressed Edit on row 2</span>
<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">updateRow</span>(<span class="tok-n">2</span>, { salary: <span class="tok-n">120000</span> }); <span class="tok-c">// user saved</span>
<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">dataBind</span>();                       <span class="tok-c">// re-sync after the change</span></code></pre></div>
<p>Filtering and sorting belong to the <strong>view</strong> (<code>view.rowFilter</code>, <code>view.sort</code>), then call <code>dataBind()</code> again. Sorting through the grid (<code>grid.sort(&quot;salary&quot;)</code>) sorts its copy; copy the direction to <code>view.sort</code> in the <code>sorted</code> event so it survives the next bind (the tutorial shows this).</p>
`,"data-source-controls":`<h3 id="51-data-source-controls">5.1 Data source controls<a class="anchor" href="#51-data-source-controls" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<p><code>SqlDataSource</code>, <code>ObjectDataSource</code>, <code>AccessDataSource</code>, <code>XmlDataSource</code> and <code>SiteMapDataSource</code> expose <code>select</code>, <code>insert</code>, <code>update</code> and <code>delete</code> and raise the matching events. There is <strong>no database driver</strong>: <code>SqlDataSource</code> calls a REST-style handler you provide, and <code>ObjectDataSource</code> calls methods on a service object. Parameters (<code>Parameter</code>, <code>ControlParameter</code>, <code>QueryStringParameter</code>, <code>SessionParameter</code>, <code>FormParameter</code>) bind values into commands. Details and runnable examples: <a href="#/api/data-sources/asp-net-to-typescript-mapping">Data sources API</a>.</p>
<hr>
`},"guide-validation":{overview:`<p>Validators register themselves with the static <code>ValidatorManager</code>, grouped by <code>validationGroup</code>. A validator reads the value of the control named in <code>controlToValidate</code>. In a browser, the manager finds it by <strong>element id</strong> (or <code>name</code>); elsewhere, register an accessor.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">ValidatorManager</span>, <span class="tok-t">RequiredFieldValidatorController</span>, <span class="tok-t">RangeValidatorController</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/core&quot;</span>;

<span class="tok-k">const</span> form = { txtName: <span class="tok-s">&quot;&quot;</span>, txtAge: <span class="tok-s">&quot;200&quot;</span> };                 <span class="tok-c">// headless: supply values yourself</span>
<span class="tok-t">ValidatorManager</span>.<span class="tok-f">registerValueAccessor</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;txtName&quot;</span>, () =&gt; form.txtName);
<span class="tok-t">ValidatorManager</span>.<span class="tok-f">registerValueAccessor</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;txtAge&quot;</span>, () =&gt; form.txtAge);

<span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">RequiredFieldValidatorController</span>({
  id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;rfvName&quot;</span>, controlToValidate: <span class="tok-s">&quot;txtName&quot;</span>, errorMessage: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Name is required.&quot;</span>, validationGroup: <span class="tok-s">&quot;person&quot;</span>,
});
<span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">RangeValidatorController</span>({
  id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;rvAge&quot;</span>, controlToValidate: <span class="tok-s">&quot;txtAge&quot;</span>, errorMessage: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Age must be 0-120.&quot;</span>,
  minimumValue: <span class="tok-n">0</span>, maximumValue: <span class="tok-n">120</span>, <span class="tok-k">type</span>: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Integer&quot;</span>, validationGroup: <span class="tok-s">&quot;person&quot;</span>,   <span class="tok-c">// type matters, see below</span>
});

console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(<span class="tok-k">await</span> <span class="tok-t">ValidatorManager</span>.<span class="tok-f">validate</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;person&quot;</span>));      <span class="tok-c">// false</span>
console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(<span class="tok-t">ValidatorManager</span>.<span class="tok-f">getInvalidValidators</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;person&quot;</span>).<span class="tok-f">map</span>((v) =&gt; v.errorMessage));
<span class="tok-c">// [ &quot;Name is required.&quot;, &quot;Age must be 0-120.&quot; ]</span>

<span class="tok-t">Object</span>.<span class="tok-f">assign</span>(form, { txtName: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Ada&quot;</span>, txtAge: <span class="tok-s">&quot;36&quot;</span> });
console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(<span class="tok-k">await</span> <span class="tok-t">ValidatorManager</span>.<span class="tok-f">validate</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;person&quot;</span>));      <span class="tok-c">// true</span></code></pre></div>
<p>Things to know:</p>
<ul><li><code>RangeValidator.type</code> defaults to <code>&quot;String&quot;</code>. Set <code>&quot;Integer&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;Double&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;Date&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;Currency&quot;</code> for numbers and dates.</li><li><code>RegularExpressionValidator</code> anchors the pattern for you (<code>^(?:...)$</code>) unless it already starts with <code>^</code> or ends with <code>$</code>. There is no flags option.</li><li><code>CustomValidator</code> takes a <strong>synchronous</strong> <code>clientValidationFunction(source, args)</code> and an <strong>async-capable</strong> <code>serverValidate(source, args)</code>. Set <code>args.isValid</code> or return a boolean. An <code>async</code> client function is ignored, so use <code>serverValidate</code> for async checks.</li><li><code>ValidationSummaryController</code> collects the messages of the invalid validators in a group (<code>getErrorMessages()</code>, <code>getFormattedErrors()</code>).</li><li><code>GridViewController</code> can validate before an update (<code>causesValidation: true</code>, <code>validationGroup</code>).</li><li>Validators with the same group accumulate for the page lifetime. Call <code>dispose()</code> on validators you recreate, or <code>ValidatorManager.clear()</code> in tests.</li></ul>
<p>Full reference: <a href="#/api/validation/web-forms-mapping">Validation API</a>.</p>
<hr>
`},"guide-login-and-security":{overview:`<p><code>SecurityManager</code> holds the active <code>IMembershipProvider</code>. Controllers (<code>LoginController</code>, <code>ChangePasswordController</code>, ...) use it unless you pass <code>provider</code>. <code>InMemoryAuthProvider</code> is included for demos and tests.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">SecurityManager</span>, <span class="tok-t">InMemoryAuthProvider</span>, <span class="tok-t">LoginController</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/core&quot;</span>;

<span class="tok-t">SecurityManager</span>.<span class="tok-f">setProvider</span>(<span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">InMemoryAuthProvider</span>({
  users: [{ userName: <span class="tok-s">&quot;ann&quot;</span>, password: <span class="tok-s">&quot;secret1&quot;</span>, roles: [<span class="tok-s">&quot;Editors&quot;</span>] }],
}));

<span class="tok-k">const</span> login = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">LoginController</span>({ id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;Login1&quot;</span> });          <span class="tok-c">// captures the provider NOW</span>
<span class="tok-k">const</span> trace: string[] = [];
login.loggingIn.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>((_s, e) =&gt; { trace.<span class="tok-f">push</span>(<span class="tok-s">\`loggingIn(\${e.userName})\`</span>); });
login.loggedIn.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>((_s, e) =&gt; { trace.<span class="tok-f">push</span>(<span class="tok-s">\`loggedIn(\${e.user.roles?.join()})\`</span>); });
login.loginError.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>(() =&gt; { trace.<span class="tok-f">push</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;loginError&quot;</span>); });

login.<span class="tok-f">setUserName</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;ann&quot;</span>); login.<span class="tok-f">setPassword</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;nope&quot;</span>);
console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(<span class="tok-k">await</span> login.<span class="tok-f">login</span>(), login.failureMessage);
<span class="tok-c">// false &quot;Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again.&quot;</span>
login.<span class="tok-f">setPassword</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;secret1&quot;</span>);
console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(<span class="tok-k">await</span> login.<span class="tok-f">login</span>(), login.currentUser?.userName, <span class="tok-t">SecurityManager</span>.defaultProvider.<span class="tok-f">isInRole</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;Editors&quot;</span>));
<span class="tok-c">// true &quot;ann&quot; true</span>
console.<span class="tok-f">log</span>(trace.<span class="tok-f">join</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot; -&gt; &quot;</span>));
<span class="tok-c">// loggingIn(ann) -&gt; loginError -&gt; loggingIn(ann) -&gt; loggedIn(Editors)</span></code></pre></div>
<p>Rules of thumb:</p>
<ul><li>Order is <code>loggingIn</code> (cancellable) → provider <code>login()</code> → <code>loggedIn</code> or <code>loginError</code>. Empty credentials fail <code>validate()</code> <strong>before</strong> any event.</li><li>Call <code>SecurityManager.setProvider(...)</code> <strong>before</strong> you create the controllers. Existing controllers keep the provider they captured.</li><li>React to sign-in/out app-wide with <code>SecurityManager.currentUserChanged.subscribe((provider, user) =&gt; ...)</code>; a custom provider must call <code>SecurityManager.notifyCurrentUserChanged(user)</code> for this to work.</li><li><code>InMemoryAuthProvider</code> locks an account after <code>maxInvalidPasswordAttempts</code> failures (default 5) and stores <strong>plain-text passwords</strong>. For a real application implement <code>IMembershipProvider</code> against your API; <a href="#/api/security/asp-net-typescript-mapping">Security API</a> contains a complete REST-backed example.</li></ul>
<hr>
`},"guide-navigation-calendar-and-other-controls":{overview:`<p><code>Menu</code>, <code>TreeView</code> and <code>SiteMapPath</code> model hierarchical data (<code>MenuItem</code>, <code>TreeNode</code>) with selection and expansion state and click/select events; they are fed by <code>SiteMapDataSource</code> or plain nested options. <code>Calendar</code> builds the 6 x 7 day matrix and raises <code>dayRender</code> for per-cell customization. <code>Xml</code> applies a transform to a document, and <code>AdRotator</code> picks advertisements by weighted lottery. Behaviors (<code>ModalBehavior</code>, <code>TabsController</code>, <code>AccordionController</code>, <code>AutoCompleteBehavior</code>, <code>ConfirmButtonBehavior</code>, <code>CollapsiblePanelBehavior</code>, <code>CascadingDropDownBehavior</code>) hold the logic of common interactive widgets.</p>
<p>References: <a href="#/api/navigation/web-forms-mapping">Navigation</a>, <a href="#/api/specialized/asp-net-typescript-mapping">Specialized controls</a>, <a href="#/api/behaviors/asp-net-typescript-mapping">Behaviors</a>.</p>
<hr>
`},"guide-ui-adapters":{react:`<h3 id="react">React<a class="anchor" href="#react" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">tsx</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-tsx"><span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">WebFormsGridView</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/react&quot;</span>;
<span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/core&quot;</span>;

<span class="tok-k">const</span> controller = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>&lt;<span class="tok-t">Product</span>&gt;({ id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;gv&quot;</span>, dataKeyField: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, columns, allowPaging: <span class="tok-k">true</span>, pageSize: <span class="tok-n">10</span> });
<span class="tok-k">await</span> controller.<span class="tok-f">dataBind</span>(products);

<span class="tok-k">export</span> <span class="tok-k">const</span> <span class="tok-t">ProductsPage</span> = () =&gt; &lt;<span class="tok-t">WebFormsGridView</span> controller={controller} /&gt;;</code></pre></div>
`,angular:`<h3 id="angular">Angular<a class="anchor" href="#angular" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">WebFormsGridViewComponent</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/angular&quot;</span>;

@<span class="tok-t">Component</span>({ standalone: <span class="tok-k">true</span>, imports: [<span class="tok-t">WebFormsGridViewComponent</span>], template: <span class="tok-s">\`&lt;wf-grid-view [controller]=&quot;grid&quot; /&gt;\`</span> })
<span class="tok-k">export</span> <span class="tok-k">class</span> <span class="tok-t">ProductsComponent</span> { grid = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>&lt;<span class="tok-t">Product</span>&gt;({ <span class="tok-c">/* ... */</span> }); }</code></pre></div>
<p>Both adapters observe the controller's <code>stateChanged</code> event and re-render. They are thin: props map to controller options and user input flows back as commands. Complete prop, slot and accessibility tables: <a href="#/api/adapters/react-installation-and-peer-dependencies">React adapters</a> and <a href="#/api/adapters/angular-installation-and-peer-dependencies">Angular adapters</a>. Several adapter features are narrower than the core controllers (for example Angular's grid has fixed action buttons); check <a href="#/api/guides/issues-ui-adapters/overview/9-ui-adapters">Known issues, section 9</a> before relying on one.</p>
<hr>
`},"guide-testing":{overview:`<p>Headless controllers are easy to test with Node's built-in runner, no DOM required. The repository's own tests live in <code>packages/*/test/*.test.mjs</code> and import the built <code>dist</code>:</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">js</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-js"><span class="tok-k">import</span> test <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;node:test&quot;</span>;
<span class="tok-k">import</span> assert <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;node:assert/strict&quot;</span>;
<span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;../dist/index.js&quot;</span>;

<span class="tok-f">test</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;cancelling rowDeleting keeps the row&quot;</span>, <span class="tok-k">async</span> () =&gt; {
  <span class="tok-k">const</span> grid = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>({ id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;g&quot;</span>, dataKeyField: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, columns: [], dataSource: [{ id: <span class="tok-n">1</span> }] });
  <span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">dataBind</span>();
  grid.rowDeleting.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>((_g, e) =&gt; { e.cancel = <span class="tok-k">true</span>; });
  assert.<span class="tok-f">equal</span>(<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">deleteRow</span>(<span class="tok-n">0</span>), <span class="tok-k">false</span>);
  assert.<span class="tok-f">equal</span>(grid.totalRecords, <span class="tok-n">1</span>);
});</code></pre></div>
<p>The Employee Manager sample shows the next two levels: a <strong>headless smoke test</strong> of the whole data/auth/validation/grid flow (<code>npm run smoke</code>) and a <strong>real-browser end-to-end test</strong> (<code>npm run e2e</code>). Remember <code>ValidatorManager.clear()</code> between tests that create validators.</p>
<hr>
`},"guide-migrating-an-asp-net-web-forms-page":{overview:`<ol><li><strong>List the controls</strong> on the <code>.aspx</code> and map each with the <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/WEBFORMS-MAPPING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">quick-reference table</a> (for example <code>asp:GridView</code> → <code>GridViewController</code>, <code>asp:RequiredFieldValidator</code> → <code>RequiredFieldValidatorController</code>).</li><li><strong>Replace code-behind events</strong> with <code>subscribe</code> calls (<code>GridView1_RowUpdating</code> → <code>grid.rowUpdating.subscribe</code>), keeping the cancel semantics (<code>e.Cancel = true</code> → <code>e.cancel = true</code>).</li><li><strong>Replace data access</strong>: <code>DataSet</code>/<code>DataTable</code> code ports almost line for line. Replace <code>SqlDataAdapter.Fill</code> with a call to your API that returns rows, then <code>table.rows.add(row)</code> for each.</li><li><strong>Replace postback flow</strong> with async calls: <code>await grid.dataBind()</code> instead of <code>DataBind()</code> inside <code>Page_Load</code>.</li><li><strong>Replace session / authentication</strong> with <code>SecurityManager</code> and a provider that talks to your server.</li><li><strong>Render</strong>: use an adapter, or write the markup from controller state as the tutorial does.</li></ol>
<p>For automated migration the <code>MIGRATION-ENGINE-SPEC.md</code> describes the mapping rules a parser/codegen should follow.</p>
<hr>
`},"guide-troubleshooting":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>TypeError: dataSource.update is not a function</code> after Edit/Delete</td><td>The grid is bound to a <code>DataTable</code></td><td>Bind <code>new DataView(table)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Grid shows the edit but the table is unchanged</td><td>Grid edits its own copy</td><td>Persist in <code>rowUpdating</code>, then re-bind</td></tr><tr><td>New rows get ids that skip numbers or repeat after reload</td><td>Auto-increment is consumed by <code>newRow()</code>; explicit ids do not advance it</td><td><code>column.resetAutoIncrement(maxId + 1)</code> after loading</td></tr><tr><td>Numeric validator accepts <code>&quot;9&quot;</code> below <code>&quot;100&quot;</code></td><td><code>RangeValidator.type</code> is <code>&quot;String&quot;</code></td><td>Set <code>type: &quot;Integer&quot;</code> / <code>&quot;Double&quot;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Cannot find module ... instanceof</code> oddities, empty grids</td><td>Two copies of <code>@wf-controls/data</code></td><td>Deduplicate (<code>npm ls @wf-controls/data</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>Login controller ignores the provider you set</td><td>Provider set after the controller was created</td><td>Call <code>SecurityManager.setProvider</code> first</td></tr><tr><td><code>LoginView</code> / <code>LoginStatus</code> do not update with a custom provider</td><td>Provider does not call <code>notifyCurrentUserChanged</code></td><td>Call it from <code>login()</code> and <code>logout()</code></td></tr><tr><td>Validators never fail in tests</td><td><code>controlToValidate</code> has no accessor or element</td><td><code>registerValueAccessor(id, () =&gt; value)</code></td></tr><tr><td>A pager or sort does nothing with a data source control</td><td>Known data-source-control paging limitation</td><td>Bind an array/<code>DataView</code>; see <a href="#/api/guides/issues-data-controls-gridview-datagrid-repeater-datalist/overview/4-data-controls-gridview-datagrid-repeater-datalist">Known issues</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<hr>
`},"guide-where-to-go-next":{overview:'<ul><li><strong>Build something:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/TUTORIAL-employee-app.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Employee Manager tutorial</a>: login, role-based permissions, grid, form, validation, full CRUD.</li><li><strong>Look something up:</strong> the API reference pages in the sidebar (every class with its properties, methods, events and parameters).</li><li><strong>Understand the limits:</strong> <a href="#/api/guides/issues-needs-your-attention-first">Known issues</a>.</li><li><strong>Older per-control guides:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/grid-view.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GridView</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/data-table-and-view.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DataTable &amp; DataView</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/validation-controls.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Validation</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/login-security.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Login &amp; security</a>, and the rest of the list in the <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">guide index</a>.</li></ul>'},"rest-three-ways-to-bind-a-rest-api":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Approach</th><th>Use it when</th><th>Paging happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>fetch()</code> then <code>grid.dataBind(array)</code></td><td>Small result sets, read-only grids</td><td>In the browser</td></tr><tr><td><code>ObjectDataSource</code> with an API class</td><td>You want select / update / delete routed through your own class</td><td>In the browser, or on the server (section 2)</td></tr><tr><td><code>SqlDataSource</code> with <code>&quot;VERB /path/{token}&quot;</code> commands</td><td>You want a declarative REST client with no API class</td><td>In the browser, or on the server (section 2)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>A plain array result is always paged in the browser: every row is held in memory and <code>visibleRows</code> is a slice.</p>
`},"rest-server-side-paging":{overview:`<p>When a data source's <code>select()</code> returns an object of the shape <code>{ items, total }</code>, the GridView switches to server-side paging:</p>
<ul><li><code>items</code> is <strong>only the requested page</strong>. The grid does not slice it again.</li><li><code>totalRecords</code> and <code>pageCount</code> come from <code>total</code>, so the pager shows the right number of pages.</li><li>The select arguments passed to your method carry <code>startRowIndex</code> (<code>pageIndex * pageSize</code>), <code>maximumRows</code> (<code>pageSize</code>) and <code>sortExpression</code> (for example <code>&quot;name ASC&quot;</code>).</li><li>Row indexes stay <strong>absolute</strong>. On page 2 with a page size of 4 the first visible row has index 4, so <code>rowDataBound</code>, <code>selectRow(i)</code>, <code>beginEdit(i)</code> and <code>deleteRow(i)</code> use the same numbers as the full data set.</li><li>Every <code>changePage</code> and <code>sort</code> calls your select method again.</li><li>A delete lowers <code>total</code> by one locally; the next <code>dataBind()</code> asks the server again.</li></ul>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">const</span> api = {
  <span class="tok-k">async</span> <span class="tok-f">page</span>(_p: unknown, args: { startRowIndex?: number; maximumRows?: number }) {
    <span class="tok-k">const</span> res = <span class="tok-k">await</span> <span class="tok-f">fetch</span>(<span class="tok-s">\`/api/employees?start=\${args.startRowIndex ?? 0}&amp;max=\${args.maximumRows ?? 50}\`</span>);
    <span class="tok-k">return</span> (<span class="tok-k">await</span> res.<span class="tok-f">json</span>()) <span class="tok-k">as</span> { items: <span class="tok-t">Employee</span>[]; total: number };
  }
};
<span class="tok-k">const</span> ds = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">ObjectDataSource</span>({ id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;employees&quot;</span>, typeInstance: api, selectMethod: <span class="tok-s">&quot;page&quot;</span> });
<span class="tok-k">const</span> grid = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>&lt;<span class="tok-t">Employee</span>&gt;({
  id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;g&quot;</span>, dataKeyField: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, allowPaging: <span class="tok-k">true</span>, pageSize: <span class="tok-n">4</span>, columns, dataSource: ds
});
<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">dataBind</span>();     <span class="tok-c">// requests start 0, max 4</span>
<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">changePage</span>(<span class="tok-n">1</span>);  <span class="tok-c">// requests start 4, max 4; grid.visibleRows holds rows 4-7</span></code></pre></div>
<p>Notes:</p>
<ul><li><code>allowPaging</code> must be <code>true</code>; without it <code>total</code> is ignored and <code>items</code> is shown whole.</li><li>Only <code>{ items, total }</code> triggers server paging. <code>DataTable</code> and <code>DataView</code> sources, and plain arrays, are paged in the browser.</li><li><code>Repeater</code> and <code>DataList</code> page in the browser only.</li></ul>
`},"rest-common-rest-problems":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pager shows one page although the server has more</td><td>Your select method returned an array</td><td>Return <code>{ items, total }</code></td></tr><tr><td>Page 2 shows the same rows as page 1</td><td>The API ignores the start index</td><td>Pass <code>args.startRowIndex</code> through</td></tr><tr><td>Row index does not match the id</td><td>You assumed page-relative indexes</td><td>Indexes are absolute; use <code>dataKeyField</code> for the key</td></tr><tr><td><code>HttpErrorResponse</code> (Angular) logged as <code>[object Object]</code></td><td>It is not an <code>Error</code></td><td>Read <code>.status</code> and <code>.message</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>See also <a href="#/api/data-binding/the-binding-model">Data Binding</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/object-data-source.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Object Data Source</a> and <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/v1.0.0/sql-data-source.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sql Data Source</a>.</p>`},"ngguide-install-and-import":{overview:`<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">bash</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-bash"><span class="tok-f">npm</span> install @wf-controls/core @wf-controls/data @wf-controls/angular</code></pre></div>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">ts</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-ts"><span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">Component</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@angular/core&quot;</span>;
<span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/core&quot;</span>;
<span class="tok-k">import</span> { <span class="tok-t">WebFormsGridViewComponent</span> } <span class="tok-k">from</span> <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/angular&quot;</span>;

@<span class="tok-t">Component</span>({
  selector: <span class="tok-s">&quot;app-employees&quot;</span>, standalone: <span class="tok-k">true</span>, imports: [<span class="tok-t">WebFormsGridViewComponent</span>],
  template: <span class="tok-s">\`&lt;wf-grid-view [controller]=&quot;grid&quot;&gt;&lt;/wf-grid-view&gt;\`</span>
})
<span class="tok-k">export</span> <span class="tok-k">class</span> <span class="tok-t">EmployeesComponent</span> {
  grid = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>&lt;<span class="tok-t">Employee</span>&gt;({ id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;g&quot;</span>, dataKeyField: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, columns, allowPaging: <span class="tok-k">true</span>, pageSize: <span class="tok-n">5</span> });
}</code></pre></div>
<p>The package is built with <code>ng-packagr</code> as partial-Ivy output (a single FESM bundle), so it works with AOT and <code>strictTemplates</code>. It requires <code>@angular/core</code> and <code>@angular/common</code> &gt;= 21.2.0 and <code>rxjs</code> &gt;= 7; Angular 21.2 is the version that was tested.</p>
`},"ngguide-signals-and-rxjs":{overview:`<p>Controllers are plain classes, not signals. The package exports the bridge: <code>viewModel(controller, project)</code> returns a signal recomputed after every <code>stateChanged</code>, <code>fromDispatcher(dispatcher)</code> returns an Observable, and <code>onEvent(dispatcher, handler)</code> subscribes for the lifetime of the component. <code>viewModel</code> and <code>onEvent</code> need an injection context (a constructor or field initialiser). In short:</p>
<ul><li>A signal that you update from <code>stateChanged</code> gives templates a reactive view of the controller.</li><li>Wrap an <code>EventDispatcher</code> in an RxJS <code>Observable</code> when you want operators; <code>subscribe</code> on a dispatcher returns an unsubscribe function, so register it with <code>DestroyRef.onDestroy</code> to prevent leaks.</li><li>Events raised from timers or <code>fetch</code> can run outside change detection; read state through a signal or call <code>markForCheck()</code>.</li></ul>
`},"ngguide-rest-with-httpclient":{overview:`<p>Give an <code>ObjectDataSource</code> an API class that wraps <code>HttpClient</code> and converts with <code>firstValueFrom</code>. For server-side paging return <code>{ items, total }</code> (<a href="#/api/guides/rest-three-ways-to-bind-a-rest-api">REST and Server-Side Paging</a>). Interceptors (<code>provideHttpClient(withInterceptors([...]))</code>) stay in Angular; the grid never sees HTTP.</p>
`},"ngguide-forms-guards-and-routing":{overview:`<ul><li>Reactive forms: build a <code>FormGroup</code> for the edit row and call <code>grid.updateRow(index, form.value)</code> on submit.</li><li>Login: keep the security controllers in a service. A functional <code>CanActivateFn</code> guard reads the current user and returns <code>router.parseUrl(&quot;/login&quot;)</code>.</li><li>After logout, navigate explicitly: the router ignores navigation to the <strong>same URL</strong>.</li><li><code>HttpErrorResponse</code> is not an <code>Error</code>; show <code>err.status</code> and <code>err.message</code>.</li><li>In tests, an <code>HttpBackend</code> override must be provided <strong>after</strong> <code>provideHttpClient</code>.</li></ul>
`},"ngguide-testing":{overview:`<p><code>ngc</code> with <code>strictTemplates</code> is the first check. For behaviour, drive the controllers directly with <code>node --test</code>. Component tests need Angular <code>TestBed</code>, which this repository does not set up.</p>
`},"ngguide-next":{overview:'<p><a href="#/api/guides/books-run-them">Books and Examples</a> (Volume 3) has 10 compiled and browser-verified examples, including a routed application. Reference: <a href="#/api/adapters/angular-installation-and-peer-dependencies">Angular adapters</a>.</p>'},"jsguide-loading-the-library":{overview:`<p>Browsers cannot resolve the bare names <code>@wf-controls/core</code> and <code>@wf-controls/data</code>, so choose one of:</p>
<p><strong>A. ES modules with an import map</strong> (needs an http server; modules do not load from <code>file://</code>)</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;script</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;importmap&quot;</span>&gt;
  { <span class="tok-s">&quot;imports&quot;</span>: { <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/core&quot;</span>: <span class="tok-s">&quot;/packages/core/dist/index.js&quot;</span>,
                 <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/data&quot;</span>: <span class="tok-s">&quot;/packages/data/dist/index.js&quot;</span> } }
<span class="tok-t">&lt;/script</span>&gt;
<span class="tok-t">&lt;script</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;module&quot;</span>&gt;
  import { GridViewController } from <span class="tok-s">&quot;@wf-controls/core&quot;</span>;
<span class="tok-t">&lt;/script</span>&gt;</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>B. One bundled script</strong> (works from <code>file://</code>): bundle your entry into a single IIFE, then load it with a normal <code>&lt;script src&gt;</code>.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">bash</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-bash"><span class="tok-f">npx</span> esbuild app.js <span class="tok-k">--bundle</span> <span class="tok-k">--format</span>=iife <span class="tok-k">--outfile</span>=app.bundle.js</code></pre></div>
`},"jsguide-the-render-pattern":{overview:`<p>A controller holds state and raises events; you re-render when it changes.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">js</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-js"><span class="tok-k">const</span> grid = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>({ id: <span class="tok-s">&quot;g&quot;</span>, dataKeyField: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, columns, allowPaging: <span class="tok-k">true</span>, pageSize: <span class="tok-n">3</span> });
<span class="tok-k">await</span> grid.<span class="tok-f">dataBind</span>(rows);
<span class="tok-k">const</span> draw = () =&gt; { tbody.innerHTML = grid.visibleRows.<span class="tok-f">map</span>(r =&gt; <span class="tok-s">\`&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;\${esc(r.name)}&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\`</span>).<span class="tok-f">join</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;&quot;</span>); };
grid.stateChanged.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>(draw);   <span class="tok-c">// returns an unsubscribe function</span>
<span class="tok-f">draw</span>();</code></pre></div>
<p>Rules that avoid bugs:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Escape every value</strong> you put into <code>innerHTML</code> (an <code>esc()</code> helper), or build nodes with <code>textContent</code>.</li><li><strong>Redraw from state</strong>, not from the click: call a command (<code>changePage</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>deleteRow</code>) and let <code>stateChanged</code> redraw.</li><li><strong>Cancel events</strong> with <code>e.cancel = true</code> inside a <code>...ing</code> handler such as <code>rowDeleting</code>.</li><li><strong>Unsubscribe</strong> the function returned by <code>subscribe</code> when you remove the element.</li><li>Use the native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> element for modals and call <code>showModal()</code>.</li></ul>
`},"jsguide-a-jquery-plugin-in-a-few-lines":{overview:`<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">js</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-js">$.fn.wfGrid = <span class="tok-k">function</span> (opts) {
  <span class="tok-k">return</span> <span class="tok-k">this</span>.<span class="tok-f">each</span>(<span class="tok-k">function</span> () {
    <span class="tok-k">const</span> $el = $(<span class="tok-k">this</span>);
    <span class="tok-k">const</span> grid = <span class="tok-k">new</span> <span class="tok-t">GridViewController</span>({ id: <span class="tok-k">this</span>.id, dataKeyField: <span class="tok-s">&quot;id&quot;</span>, ...opts });
    grid.rowDeleting.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>((_s, e) =&gt; {
      <span class="tok-k">const</span> ev = $.<span class="tok-t">Event</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;wf:beforeDelete&quot;</span>);
      $el.<span class="tok-f">trigger</span>(ev, e);
      <span class="tok-k">if</span> (ev.<span class="tok-f">isDefaultPrevented</span>()) e.cancel = <span class="tok-k">true</span>;   <span class="tok-c">// preventDefault() cancels the delete</span>
    });
    grid.stateChanged.<span class="tok-f">subscribe</span>(() =&gt; <span class="tok-f">render</span>($el, grid));
    grid.<span class="tok-f">dataBind</span>(opts.data).<span class="tok-f">then</span>(() =&gt; <span class="tok-f">render</span>($el, grid));
    $el.<span class="tok-f">data</span>(<span class="tok-s">&quot;wfGrid&quot;</span>, grid);                          <span class="tok-c">// expose the controller</span>
  });
};</code></pre></div>
<p>jQuery is a classic script that defines <code>window.jQuery</code>; load it before your module.</p>
`},"jsguide-roles-and-validation-in-the-dom":{overview:`<p>Show or hide elements by role with <code>data-role=&quot;admin&quot;</code> and a loop that reads the signed-in user's roles. For validation, run one validator per field, aggregate the results, then set <code>aria-invalid</code> once per field so a later passing validator cannot clear an earlier failure.</p>
`},"jsguide-styling-plain-html-js":{overview:`<p><code>@wf-controls/styles</code> is plain CSS, so a <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> is all you need. Each theme has two bundles: <code>&lt;theme&gt;-full.css</code> (all ten families: the kit's seven plus Modal, Repeater, DataList and the grid edit-row sheet; recommended) and <code>&lt;theme&gt;-all.css</code> (the kit's seven families only); every rule is scoped to a class such as <code>gv-modern</code>, so several themes can coexist on a page.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;link</span><span class="tok-k"> rel</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;stylesheet&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;node_modules/@wf-controls/styles/css/bundles/modern-full.css&quot;</span> /&gt;
<span class="tok-c">&lt;!-- minified: node_modules/@wf-controls/styles/dist/css/bundles/modern-full.min.css --&gt;</span>
<span class="tok-c">&lt;!-- kit only (no modal / repeater / datalist / edit-row sheet): .../css/bundles/modern-all.css --&gt;</span>
<span class="tok-c">&lt;!-- one family only: node_modules/@wf-controls/styles/css/gridview/gv-modern.css --&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
<p>Themes: <code>modern</code>, <code>dark</code>, <code>classic</code>, <code>minimal</code>, <code>corporate</code>. Families: GridView (<code>gv-</code>), Login family (<code>lg-</code>), Menu (<code>mn-</code>), TreeView (<code>tv-</code>), Tabs (<code>tb-</code>), Navigation (<code>nv-</code>: SiteMapPath, DataPager, link list) Validation (<code>vl-</code>), and three added families: popup dialog (<code>md-</code>), Repeater (<code>rp-</code>) and DataList (<code>dl-</code>), plus <code>gv-&lt;theme&gt;-edit.css</code> for form controls in grid edit rows. Calendar, Accordion and AdRotator are not covered. To switch theme, load the other bundle and change the one class on the control root (<code>gv-modern</code> to <code>gv-dark</code>).</p>
<p>You write the markup, so follow the contract. You do <strong>not</strong> need <code>adapters.css</code> (that file only exists to adapt the React/Angular list-and-button markup).</p>
<p><strong>GridView</strong> (the table carries the theme; <code>selected</code>, <code>edit</code>, <code>footer</code>, <code>pager</code>, <code>empty</code> are row classes):</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;table</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;gv-modern&quot;</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;tr</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;th</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;#&quot;</span>&gt;Name<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/th</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;th</span>&gt;Dept<span class="tok-t">&lt;/th</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;th</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/th</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/tr</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;tr</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;Ada<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;Eng<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;#&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;btn-link&quot;</span>&gt;Edit<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;#&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;btn-link text-danger&quot;</span>&gt;Delete<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/tr</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;tr</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;selected&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;Grace<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;Eng<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/tr</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;tr</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;pager&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span><span class="tok-k"> colspan</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;3&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;span</span>&gt;1<span class="tok-t">&lt;/span</span>&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;#&quot;</span>&gt;2<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/tr</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;tr</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;empty&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span><span class="tok-k"> colspan</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;3&quot;</span>&gt;No records found.<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/tr</span>&gt;   <span class="tok-c">&lt;!-- only when there is no data --&gt;</span>
<span class="tok-t">&lt;/table</span>&gt;</code></pre></div>
<p>For an inline edit row (and the insert row) use <code>tr.edit</code> / <code>tr.footer</code>. Besides text and date inputs, <code>select</code>, <code>textarea</code>, number / email / untyped <code>input</code>, checkbox, <code>label</code> and <code>button</code> are styled by the edit-row sheet (in <code>-full.css</code>, not in <code>-all.css</code>):</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;tr</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;edit&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;input</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;text&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> value</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;Ada&quot;</span> /&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;select</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;option</span>&gt;Eng<span class="tok-t">&lt;/option</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;option</span>&gt;Ops<span class="tok-t">&lt;/option</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/select</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;label</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;input</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;checkbox&quot;</span> checked /&gt; Active<span class="tok-t">&lt;/label</span>&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span>&gt;Save<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span>&gt;Cancel<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/td</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/tr</span>&gt;</code></pre></div>
<p>Build it from the controller: <code>grid.visibleRows</code> for the rows, <code>grid.options.selectedIndex</code> / <code>editIndex</code> for the <code>selected</code> / <code>edit</code> classes, and <code>grid.pageCount</code> for the pager. The kit's pager selector expects a nested table in the pager cell; the flat form above is what the React and Angular adapters emit.</p>
<p><strong>Menu</strong> (horizontal; add <code>mn-vertical</code> for vertical; <code>ul.dynamic</code> is the flyout, you show and hide it):</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;mn-modern&quot;</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;ul</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;static&quot;</span>&gt;
    <span class="tok-t">&lt;li</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;selected&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;/&quot;</span>&gt;Home<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/li</span>&gt;
    <span class="tok-t">&lt;li</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;has-popup&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;#&quot;</span>&gt;Products<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt;
      <span class="tok-t">&lt;ul</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;dynamic&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;li</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;/hw&quot;</span>&gt;Hardware<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/li</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/ul</span>&gt;
    <span class="tok-t">&lt;/li</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;/ul</span>&gt;
<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>TreeView</strong> (labels <code>a.root</code> / <code>a.parent</code> / <code>a.leaf</code> plus <code>selected</code>; the child container id must end in <code>Nodes</code>):</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;tv-modern&quot;</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;root parent&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;#&quot;</span>&gt;Company<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> id</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;tree1Nodes&quot;</span>&gt;
    <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;a</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;leaf selected&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> href</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;#&quot;</span>&gt;Engineering<span class="tok-t">&lt;/a</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Modal</strong> (<code>ModalBehavior</code>; you render the overlay while <code>modal.isOpen</code> and wire Escape, backdrop click, focus and scroll lock yourself, as the React and Angular adapters do):</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;modal fade show d-block md-modern&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> role</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;dialog&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> aria-modal</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;true&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> aria-labelledby</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;dlg-title&quot;</span>
    <span class="tok-k"> style</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;background-color: var(--wf-backdrop, rgba(0,0,0,.5))&quot;</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;modal-content shadow&quot;</span>&gt;
    <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;modal-header&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;h5</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;modal-title&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> id</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;dlg-title&quot;</span>&gt;Delete employee<span class="tok-t">&lt;/h5</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;btn-close&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> aria-label</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;Close&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
    <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;modal-body&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;label</span><span class="tok-k"> for</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;reason&quot;</span>&gt;Reason<span class="tok-t">&lt;/label</span>&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;input</span><span class="tok-k"> id</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;reason&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;text&quot;</span> /&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
    <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;modal-footer&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot;</span>&gt;Cancel<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;</span>&gt;OK<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;</code></pre></div>
<p>The sheet makes <code>div.modal</code> a full-viewport overlay and draws the close glyph with CSS (keep <code>btn-close</code> empty). Change the backdrop with the <code>--wf-backdrop</code> variable (<code>.md-dark { --wf-backdrop: rgba(0,0,0,.75) }</code>). Dismiss on Escape and on a click on the overlay (call <code>modal.handleCancel()</code>), move focus into the dialog on <code>shown</code>, cycle Tab inside it, set <code>document.body.style.overflow = &quot;hidden&quot;</code> while open and restore focus on <code>hidden</code>; or use the native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> element instead and skip the <code>md-</code> family.</p>
<p><strong>Repeater</strong> (<code>div.wf-repeater</code>; items <code>div.wf-item</code>, odd ones also <code>alt</code>, the current one <code>active</code>, the one in edit mode <code>edit</code>):</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;wf-repeater rp-modern&quot;</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;add&quot;</span>&gt;Add item<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;wf-item&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;header</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;wf-item-header&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;span</span>&gt;Item 1<span class="tok-t">&lt;/span</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span>&gt;Delete<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/header</span>&gt;Ada<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;wf-item alt active&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;header</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;wf-item-header&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;span</span>&gt;Item 2<span class="tok-t">&lt;/span</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/header</span>&gt;Grace<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;wf-item edit&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;input</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;text&quot;</span> /&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;select</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/select</span>&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span>&gt;Save<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span>&gt;Cancel<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-c">&lt;!-- no items: &lt;div class=&quot;empty&quot;&gt;No records found.&lt;/div&gt; --&gt;</span>
<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>DataList</strong> (Flow layout is <code>div.wf-datalist</code>, Table layout is <code>table.datalist-table.wf-datalist</code>; the semantic classes <code>alt</code>, <code>selected</code>, <code>edit</code>, <code>header</code>, <code>footer</code>, <code>separator</code> go next to <code>datalist-&lt;type&gt;</code>):</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">html</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-html"><span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;wf-datalist dl-modern&quot;</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;datalist-item&quot;</span>&gt;Ada<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;datalist-item datalist-alternatingitem alt&quot;</span>&gt;Grace<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;datalist-item datalist-selecteditem selected&quot;</span>&gt;Linus<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
  <span class="tok-t">&lt;div</span><span class="tok-k"> class</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;datalist-item datalist-edititem edit&quot;</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;input</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;text&quot;</span> /&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span>&gt;Save<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt; <span class="tok-t">&lt;button</span><span class="tok-k"> type</span>=<span class="tok-s">&quot;button&quot;</span>&gt;Cancel<span class="tok-t">&lt;/button</span>&gt;<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
<span class="tok-t">&lt;/div</span>&gt;
<span class="tok-c">&lt;!-- Table layout: &lt;table class=&quot;datalist-table wf-datalist dl-modern&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;datalist-cell datalist-item&quot;&gt;..&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;; empty: &lt;p class=&quot;empty&quot;&gt;No items.&lt;/p&gt; --&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
<p>Inside the Repeater and DataList edit items the <code>rp-</code> / <code>dl-</code> families style <code>input</code>, <code>select</code>, <code>textarea</code>, checkbox, <code>label</code> and <code>button</code>. A button is accent-coloured when it is <code>.add</code>, <code>.save</code>, <code>.primary</code>, <code>[type=submit]</code>, <code>[data-command=Update|Save|Insert]</code> or the first button of the edit item; <code>.delete</code> / <code>[data-command=Delete]</code> is red. The runnable version of all of this is example 11 (<code>docs/book/examples-js/ex11-themes.js</code>).</p>
<p>The full contract for every family (Login, Tabs, Navigation, Validation) and the controller-option-to-class table are in <code>packages/styles/README.md</code>. Validation: put <code>vl-&lt;theme&gt;</code> on a validator message <code>span</code> or a summary <code>div</code> and add <code>is-invalid</code> to the offending input. <code>validation-input-highlight.js</code> only works with the ASP.NET <code>WebUIValidation</code> globals, so toggle <code>is-invalid</code> yourself from the validator's result.</p>
`},"jsguide-where-to-go-next":{overview:'<ul><li>Runnable examples and the full chapter set: <a href="#/api/guides/books-run-them">Books and Examples</a> (Volume 4).</li><li>API: <a href="#/api/data-controls/asp-net-to-typescript-mapping">Data Controls</a>, <a href="#/api/validation/web-forms-mapping">Validation</a>.</li></ul>'},"books-run-them":{overview:`<p>Run every command from the repository root.</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">bash</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-bash"><span class="tok-f">npm</span> install &amp;&amp; npm run build                     <span class="tok-c"># once</span>
<span class="tok-f">node</span> docs/book/examples/serve.mjs                <span class="tok-c"># React gallery   http://localhost:4100</span>
<span class="tok-f">node</span> docs/book/examples-angular/serve.mjs        <span class="tok-c"># Angular gallery http://localhost:4300 (/?app = routed app)</span>
<span class="tok-f">node</span> docs/book/examples-js/serve.mjs             <span class="tok-c"># JS gallery      http://localhost:8080/docs/book/examples-js/gallery.html</span></code></pre></div>
<p>The Angular examples and the jQuery example need extra packages. Install them in <strong>one</strong> command, because separate <code>--no-save</code> installs prune each other:</p>
<div class="code-block"><div class="code-head"><span class="code-lang">bash</span><button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre><code class="lang-bash"><span class="tok-f">npm</span> install <span class="tok-k">--no-save</span> @angular/forms@21.2.23 @angular/router@21.2.23 jquery@3.7.1</code></pre></div>
<p>Full requirements, ports and troubleshooting: <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/book/RUNNING-THE-EXAMPLES.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/book/RUNNING-THE-EXAMPLES.md</a>.</p>
`},"books-verify-them":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Command</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Library tests</td><td><code>npm test</code></td></tr><tr><td>Angular AOT and 10 browser scenarios</td><td><code>node docs/book/examples-angular/verify/run.mjs</code></td></tr><tr><td>JavaScript 10 browser scenarios</td><td><code>node docs/book/examples-js/verify/run.mjs</code></td></tr><tr><td>CLI demos (15)</td><td><code>npm run demo -w wf-controls-demo-showcase</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Only Chrome was tested.</p>
`},"books-rebuild-a-pdf":{overview:`<p><code>node docs/book/build-book.mjs --book vol3</code> (<code>vol1</code> to <code>vol5</code>). Needs Chrome; set <code>PDFJS_PATH</code> to a <code>pdfjs-dist</code> install to get page numbers in the table of contents. See <a href="https://github.com/ahsan-wolf/webforms-ts-controls/blob/main/docs/book/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/book/README.md</a>.</p>
`},"books-related-guides":{overview:'<p><a href="#/api/guides/rest-three-ways-to-bind-a-rest-api">REST and Server-Side Paging</a> · <a href="#/api/guides/ngguide-install-and-import">Angular Guide</a> · <a href="#/api/guides/jsguide-loading-the-library">JavaScript / HTML Guide</a></p>'},"issues-needs-your-attention-first":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Area</th><th>Issue</th><th>Workaround</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Core</td><td><strong>bug:</strong> <code>packages/core/src/naming/</code> (<code>NamingContainer</code>, <code>ClientID</code>/<code>UniqueID</code>) is empty: both source files are 0 bytes, nothing is exported from <code>index.ts</code>, and the test file is empty too, although commit <code>d03e63b</code> and the project notes describe it as implemented.</td><td>Treat NamingContainer as <strong>not implemented</strong>. Use your own id scheme.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>GridView</td><td><del><strong>bug:</strong> bound directly to a <code>DataTable</code>, <code>sort()</code>, <code>changePage()</code>, <code>updateRow()</code> and <code>deleteRow()</code> misbehaved.</del> <strong>Fixed:</strong> <code>GridViewController</code> and <code>RepeaterController</code> no longer mistake a <code>DataTable</code> / <code>DataView</code> for a data-source control.</td><td>Binding a <code>DataView</code> is still the way to filter or sort at the source.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>GridView</td><td><strong>gotcha:</strong> <code>dataBind()</code> copies rows out of the <code>DataTable</code> (<code>row.toObject()</code>). Edits and deletes done through the grid change only that copy.</td><td>Write changes to the <code>DataTable</code> yourself in <code>rowUpdating</code> / <code>rowDeleting</code>, then re-bind.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Security</td><td><code>InMemoryAuthProvider</code> stores passwords as <strong>plain text</strong> and builds temporary passwords with <code>Math.random()</code>. <code>rememberMe</code> is ignored.</td><td>Demo/test only. Implement <code>IMembershipProvider</code> against your server.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Security</td><td><code>LoginController.login()</code> does <strong>not</strong> call <code>authenticate()</code> or <code>validateUser()</code>; there is no &quot;authenticate&quot; event. The real order is <code>loggingIn</code> → <code>provider.login()</code> → <code>loggedIn</code> / <code>loginError</code>.</td><td>Do extra checks in <code>loggingIn</code> and set <code>e.cancel = true</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Validation</td><td><strong>gotcha:</strong> <code>RangeValidator.type</code> defaults to <code>&quot;String&quot;</code>, so numeric ranges compare as text (<code>&quot;9&quot; &gt; &quot;100&quot;</code>).</td><td>Always pass <code>type: &quot;Integer&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;Double&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;Date&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;Currency&quot;</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<hr>
`},"issues-data-library-wf-controls-data":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>limitation</td><td><code>DataColumn.unique</code> and <code>DataTable.primaryKey</code> are <strong>never enforced</strong>: duplicate keys are accepted, and only <code>find()</code> reads <code>primaryKey</code>. Enforce uniqueness yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><code>allowDBNull: false</code> is checked only in <code>setItem</code>. A new row whose default is <code>null</code> is added without any check.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>The auto-increment value is taken in the <code>DataRow</code> constructor, so every <code>newRow()</code> / <code>rows.add({...})</code> consumes one, even if the row is later discarded. Explicit ids do not advance the counter. After loading saved rows call <code>column.resetAutoIncrement(maxId + 1)</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Columns added after rows exist are not back-filled (<code>row.item(newCol)</code> is <code>undefined</code>, not the default).</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Boolean coercion is <code>Boolean(value)</code>, so the string <code>&quot;false&quot;</code> becomes <code>true</code>. Date coercion goes through <code>String()</code>, so a numeric epoch throws.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Setting a column back to its original value with <code>setItem</code> / <code>setValues</code> leaves the row <code>Modified</code>; only <code>row.rejectChanges()</code> returns it to <code>Unchanged</code>, so build undo on <code>rejectChanges()</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>DataTable.copy()</code> turns <code>Modified</code> rows into <code>Added</code> and loses original values. <code>DataRowCollection.remove()</code> / <code>removeAt()</code> leave <code>rowState</code> unchanged. <code>rows.add()</code> has no duplicate check.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>DataTable.fromObjects</code> infers column types from the <strong>first object only</strong>. A <code>null</code> first value makes the column <code>&quot;string&quot;</code>; keys appearing only in later objects are dropped.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td>Filter expressions support only <code>field op literal</code> joined by <code>AND</code> / <code>OR</code>: no parentheses, <code>IN</code>, <code>IS NULL</code> or <code>NOT</code>. The parser splits on <code>AND</code> / <code>OR</code> even inside quoted strings, <code>LIKE</code> does not escape regex characters (<code>'%(%'</code> throws), and <code>null</code> compares as <code>0</code> in <code>&lt;</code> / <code>&gt;</code>. Use a predicate function for anything complex.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>A sort-expression direction other than <code>ASC</code> (for example a typo) silently acts as <code>DESC</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>DataView.toRows()</code> with a <strong>string</strong> <code>rowFilter</code> drops <code>Deleted</code> rows even if <code>rowStateFilter</code> includes <code>&quot;Deleted&quot;</code>. <code>find()</code> / <code>findRows()</code> use strict <code>===</code> and a linear scan. <code>toTable()</code> drops defaults, auto-increment and keys.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>DataSet.toJson()</code> loses auto-increment, seed/step, read-only, max length, caption, unique, primary key, relations and row states. <code>fromJson()</code> can throw if a <code>null</code> sits in an <code>allowDBNull: false</code> column.</td></tr><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>DataSet.toXml()</code> writes dates with <code>String(date)</code> (locale dependent, not ISO). <code>fromXml()</code> is regex based: every value comes back as a string, attributes and self-closing tags are not supported, and unescaping <code>&amp;amp;</code> first double-decodes (<code>&amp;lt;</code> round-trips as <code>&lt;</code>).</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>DataRelation.getParentRow</code> lets a <code>null</code> child key match a parent row whose key is <code>null</code>; the constructor does not check that the columns exist. <code>DataTableCollection</code>'s name index goes stale if a table is renamed after <code>add()</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
`},"issues-data-sources":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>XmlDataSource</code> Node fallback (no <code>DOMParser</code>): with no <code>xPath</code> it returns <code>[]</code> for ordinary documents, a self-closing element swallows the next sibling, and text-only elements are dropped. In the browser the DOM path is used and behaves correctly.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><code>XmlDataSource</code> XPath keeps only the first path segment (<code>/catalog/book</code> selects <code>catalog</code>) and supports no predicates. It does not check the HTTP status when loading <code>dataFile</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>SqlDataSource</code> default REST handler treats any <code>WORD rest</code> command as <code>METHOD url</code>, so plain SQL such as <code>SELECT * FROM T</code> issues an HTTP method named <code>SELECT</code>. Plain SQL needs a custom <code>handler</code>. It also prefixes <code>connectionString</code> even to absolute URLs, and turns an unknown <code>{token}</code> into an empty string without an error.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>SqlDataSource</code>'s <code>deleting</code> event exposes no parameter bag, so a handler cannot change what is sent; <code>ObjectDataSource</code> does use <code>deleting.keys</code>. Declared select parameters beat <code>selectArgs</code> in <code>SqlDataSource</code>, but <code>selectArgs</code> overwrites them in <code>ObjectDataSource</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>AccessDataSource.delete({})</code> and <code>update({}, values)</code> match <strong>every row</strong>. It calls <code>acceptChanges()</code> after each write (wiping row-state tracking), ignores <code>initialData</code> when <code>table</code> is given, infers column types from the first row only, and silently ignores unknown columns on insert.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>SiteMapDataSource</code> mutates its input nodes (adds circular <code>parent</code> links), so <code>JSON.stringify</code> of the result throws; links parents only in the constructor (assigning <code>siteMap</code> later breaks breadcrumbs); ignores <code>roles</code> (no security trimming); falls back to the root when <code>startingNodeUrl</code> is not found.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>Parameter</code> ignores its <code>defaultValue</code> argument when an options object is passed. <code>QueryStringParameter</code> / <code>SessionParameter</code> skip the browser fallback once a context object is supplied.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td>Declared but unused: <code>selectCommandType</code>, <code>typeName</code>, <code>dataFilePath</code>, <code>Parameter.direction</code> / <code>size</code>, <code>retrieveTotalRowCount</code> / <code>totalRowCount</code>. There is no caching, <code>ConvertEmptyStringToNull</code>, <code>CancelSelectOnNullParameter</code>, or Cookie/Profile/Route parameter.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
`},"issues-data-controls-gridview-datagrid-repeater-datalist":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>fixed</td><td>GridView bound to a data source control with paging used to stay on one page. Now, when <code>select()</code> returns <code>{ items, total }</code>, the grid does server-side paging (<code>totalRecords</code> / <code>pageCount</code> come from <code>total</code>, <code>items</code> is the current page, indexes stay absolute). A plain array result is still paged client-side.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>GridView</code> and <code>Repeater</code> remember the argument to <code>dataBind(arg)</code>; <code>DataGrid</code> and <code>DataList</code> do not (a later <code>dataBind()</code> rebinds the constructor source, or empties the control if there is none).</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>DataGrid</code> and <code>DataList</code> accept only an array from a data source's <code>select()</code>; a <code>DataTable</code>, <code>DataView</code> or <code>{ items }</code> result becomes empty. <code>GridView</code> and <code>Repeater</code> accept all of them.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>DataGrid</code> <code>itemCreated</code> / <code>itemDataBound</code> use page-relative indexes while every command and state method uses absolute indexes. <code>dataBinding.itemCount</code> is always <code>0</code> for DataGrid and DataList.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>DataGrid.pageIndexChanged</code> and <code>sortCommand</code> fire <strong>before</strong> the change and are cancellable; <code>GridView</code>'s <code>pageIndexChanged</code> / <code>sorted</code> args carry a <code>cancel</code> field that is ignored.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Descending sort puts <code>null</code> / <code>undefined</code> first. An in-memory re-bind does not re-apply the remembered <code>currentSort</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>GridView.deleteRow</code> does not adjust <code>selectedIndex</code> / <code>editIndex</code>; <code>updateRow</code> clears <code>editIndex</code> whichever row was updated; <code>beginEdit(j)</code> while editing row <code>i</code> switches silently with no cancel event.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>Repeater</code>: <code>deleteItem</code>, <code>addItem</code> and <code>updateItem</code> are not cancellable and do not call the data source; <code>executeCommand</code> does not route <code>Delete</code> / <code>Update</code>. <code>DataList.selectItem(-1)</code> cannot deselect. <code>DataList</code>'s <code>Header</code> / <code>Footer</code> / <code>Separator</code> item types are declared but never produced (<code>Repeater</code> does raise <code>itemCreated</code> for them, without a <code>dataItem</code>).</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td>Never read by the controllers: <code>sortable</code>, <code>visible</code>, <code>format</code>, <code>readOnly</code>, <code>dataSourceId</code>, <code>repeatLayout</code>, <code>allowUserToAddItems</code>, <code>allowUserToDeleteItems</code> and <code>itemHeaderVisible</code>. The controllers do not read the CSS-class options either; the React and Angular <strong>adapters</strong> do (GridView classes in both; <code>itemCssClass</code> / <code>alternatingItemCssClass</code> in the React and Angular Repeater). <code>sortable: false</code> does <strong>not</strong> block <code>sort()</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>pageSize: 0</code> on GridView gives <code>pageCount = Infinity</code>. The <code>DataGrid</code> <code>pageSize</code> setter is not clamped (only its constructor is).</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>events.ts</code> has <code>CancelEventArgs</code> and per-control argument <strong>interfaces</strong>, not classes; there is no generic <code>CommandEventArgs</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
`},"issues-validation":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>RequiredFieldValidator</code>: passing only <code>text</code> leaves <code>errorMessage</code> as &quot;Input is invalid.&quot; (the &quot;This field is required.&quot; default applies only when neither is given). <code>text</code> is copied from <code>errorMessage</code> once, at construction.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>RegularExpressionValidator</code>: a pattern with only a leading <code>^</code> or only a trailing <code>$</code> is not anchored on the other side (<code>&quot;^\\d+&quot;</code> matches <code>&quot;123abc&quot;</code>). There is no flags option; an invalid pattern, including .NET-style <code>(?i)</code>, silently returns invalid.</td></tr><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>CustomValidator</code>: an <code>async</code> <strong><code>clientValidationFunction</code></strong> returns a Promise that is ignored, so the field counts as valid. Put async checks in <code>serverValidate</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Double and Currency conversion uses lenient <code>parseFloat</code>, so <code>&quot;12abc&quot;</code> counts as <code>12</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Disabling a validator that already failed leaves <code>isValid</code> <code>false</code>, so <code>ValidatorManager.isValid</code> and <code>ValidationSummary</code> stay stale until you re-validate or call <code>reset</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>BaseValidator.validate()</code> re-reads the control value after evaluation, outside the try/catch, so a throwing accessor rejects <code>validate()</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><code>display</code>, <code>setFocusOnError</code> and <code>showSummary</code> are stored but never acted on by the core.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
`},"issues-navigation":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>limitation</td><td><code>Menu</code> <code>orientation</code> / <code>disappearAfter</code>, <code>TreeView</code> <code>showLines</code> and <code>SiteMapPath</code> <code>showToolTips</code> are stored but never acted on. The <code>Menu</code> constructor clamps <code>staticDisplayLevels</code> and <code>maximumDynamicDisplayLevels</code>; later assignment does not.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><code>TreeView</code> has <strong>no check propagation</strong> (parent/child); <code>checkNode</code> ignores <code>shouldShowCheckBox</code>; <code>selected: true</code> in node options does not set <code>selectedNode</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>findItem</code> / <code>findNode</code> match <code>valuePath</code>, <code>value</code> or <code>text</code>, first in pre-order, so duplicates are ambiguous. <code>depth</code> and <code>valuePath</code> are <code>0</code> / <code>&quot;&quot;</code> until <code>refreshHierarchy</code>. <code>fromSiteMapNode</code> drops <code>roles</code> and other flags.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>SiteMapPath.dataBind</code> stores an unknown <code>currentUrlOrKey</code> even when the lookup fails and returns the internal array (<code>getItems()</code> returns a copy). There is no separator item type.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
`},"issues-login-security":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Controllers capture <code>SecurityManager.defaultProvider</code> in their <strong>constructor</strong>: a later <code>setProvider()</code> does not re-point existing controllers. <code>LoginView</code>, <code>LoginStatus</code> and <code>LoginName</code> listen to the global <code>currentUserChanged</code> regardless of provider.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>A custom provider must call <code>SecurityManager.notifyCurrentUserChanged(user)</code> itself, or <code>LoginView</code>, <code>LoginStatus</code> and <code>LoginName</code> will not refresh.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>LoginController.getState()</code> and <code>ChangePasswordController.getState()</code> call <code>validate()</code>, overwriting <code>validationErrors</code>. <code>LoginStatus</code> emits <code>stateChanged</code> twice on logout.</td></tr><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>PasswordRecovery</code>: cancelling <code>sendingMail</code> does not undo the provider's password reset, and no mail is ever sent by the controller.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>InMemoryAuthProvider.createUser</code> trims the user name but lookups only lower-case it, so a padded name can never log in. <code>changePassword</code> does not check lock-out. <code>InvalidQuestion</code>, <code>InvalidAnswer</code>, <code>InvalidEmail</code>, <code>UserRejected</code> and <code>ProviderError</code> are never returned by the in-memory provider.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Several emits are not awaited (<code>stateChanged</code>, <code>viewChanged</code>, <code>continueButtonClick</code>, <code>CollapsiblePanelBehavior.stateChanged</code>), so errors thrown by async handlers surface as unhandled rejections.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
`},"issues-specialized-controls-behaviors":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>Calendar</code> <code>dayRender</code> copies <code>args.cellText</code>, <code>customMarkup</code>, <code>cssClass</code> and <code>isSelectable</code> back over <code>args.day.*</code>, so edits made directly on <code>args.day</code> are lost. <code>selectDate</code>, <code>selectWeek</code> and <code>selectMonth</code> now respect <code>isSelectable</code> set in <code>dayRender</code> (fixed), but still ignore <code>isOtherMonth</code>. <code>nextPrevFormat</code> has no effect.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><code>Xml</code>: <code>documentSource</code> and <code>transformSource</code>, and <code>AdRotator.advertisementFile</code>, are stored but never used. XSLT support is a tiny regex subset (<code>xsl:value-of select=&quot;.&quot;</code> yields an empty string); output is <strong>not HTML-escaped</strong>, and neither is <code>AdRotator.render()</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>AdRotator</code> impressions of <code>NaN</code> are not sanitized, so selection falls back to the first ad.</td></tr><tr><td>bug</td><td><code>TabsController</code>: <code>onActiveTabChanged</code> is accepted but never invoked; <code>setActiveTab</code> ignores <code>enabled</code> / <code>visible</code>. <code>AccordionController.setSelectedIndex</code> has no bounds check.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>ConfirmButtonBehavior.execute()</code> returns <code>true</code> without calling <code>onConfirm</code> when <code>window.confirm</code> is unavailable (Node/SSR). <code>ModalBehavior.handleOk</code> still runs <code>onOk</code> when the modal is closed. No behavior event is cancellable.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><code>AutoCompleteBehavior</code>: <code>completionInterval</code>, <code>completionSetCount</code> and <code>serviceMethod</code> are unused; the cache never expires and there is no debounce or stale-response guard.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
`},"issues-ui-adapters":{overview:`<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>ng-packagr</code> 21 rejects TypeScript 6, so <code>packages/angular</code> is built with TypeScript 5.9 (its own devDependency). Installing the published package into a fresh <code>ng new</code> app was not run; the sample app imports the adapter source path.</td></tr><tr><td>fixed</td><td>The Angular grid used to ignore <code>tableCssClass</code>, the row/header/footer/pager classes and <code>showFooter</code>; React <code>NavigationMenu</code>, <code>TreeView</code> and <code>Breadcrumb</code> used to ignore their controllers (and rendered no flyouts, <code>selected</code> or <code>separator</code>); <code>WebFormsTabs</code> ignored <code>visible</code> and emitted no <code>aria-controls</code>; React <code>NavigationMenu</code> <code>className</code> applied to horizontal menus only; <code>WebFormsGridView</code> kept staged edit values after a save. All of these are now implemented (see the adapter references).</td></tr><tr><td>fixed</td><td><code>grid-view.md</code> section 4 showed an Angular <code>#template</code> slot and <code>[(ngModel)]</code> that the component does not implement. It now documents the real <code>#editTemplate</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td>Angular <code>wf-grid-view</code> has no user template-column slot (the action column is three fixed links: Select, Edit, Delete). Without <code>#editTemplate</code>, Edit enters edit mode (the row gets class <code>edit</code>) but its cells show no editor. <code>wf-repeater</code> supports only item / edit-item templates. For <code>wf-grid-view</code> and <code>wf-repeater</code>, a controller <code>@Input</code> swap after init is not re-subscribed (the six newer Angular components do re-subscribe).</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td>Angular <code>wf-menu</code>: a cancel in <code>menuItemClick</code> blocks selection and <code>itemClick</code> but cannot stop native anchor navigation (same for React <code>NavigationMenu</code> in controller mode), and nested static levels render as sibling <code>li</code> elements. <code>wf-tabs</code> needs <code>refresh()</code> after <code>TabsController.setTabs()</code> (it emits nothing). Angular adapters exist only for GridView, Repeater, DataList, Tabs, Modal, TreeView, Breadcrumb and Menu; there is no <code>&lt;wf-data-grid&gt;</code> and no React <code>WebFormsDataGrid</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>React <code>Breadcrumb</code> shows demo items when neither <code>items</code> nor <code>controller</code> is given. React <code>NavigationMenu</code> <code>orientation</code> is lower-case (<code>&quot;horizontal&quot;</code>), core <code>MenuOrientation</code> is title-case; a <code>controller</code> overrides the prop. React <code>TreeView</code> plain mode has no checkboxes and <code>onNodeClick</code> / <code>onNodeToggle</code> are not called in controller mode.</td></tr><tr><td>fixed</td><td>React <code>WebFormsModal</code> used to have no Escape / backdrop handling, no <code>aria-modal</code> / <code>aria-labelledby</code> and no focus management; it now cancels on Escape and backdrop click, sets <code>aria-modal</code> and <code>aria-labelledby</code>, traps Tab, locks body scroll and returns focus (the Angular <code>wf-modal</code> matches).</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>React <code>WebFormsModal</code> still reads <code>behavior.isOpen</code> only on mount, so a recreated behavior instance does not open a dialog shown through the old one; keep the instance stable (<code>useMemo</code> / <code>useRef</code>).</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><code>WebFormsGridView</code>: <code>cssClass</code> is applied to both the wrapper and the table (intended for the kit: <code>cssClass: &quot;gv-modern&quot;</code>); the default editor always writes strings and has <strong>no Save button</strong> (it renders inputs only), so supply <code>editTemplate</code> or <code>editCellTemplate</code>. The pager is shown whenever <code>allowPaging</code> is on, even for one page, with hard-coded English labels.</td></tr><tr><td>packaging</td><td><code>packages/react</code> lists <code>@types/react</code> only as a dev dependency and was not re-checked for <code>files</code> / <code>exports</code> (<code>packages/angular</code> has both). There is no <code>packages/jquery</code>: plain HTML uses the core directly (older notes that mention <code>@wf-controls/jquery</code> or <code>$.fn.wf*</code> plugins were wrong and have been corrected).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
`},"issues-styling-kit-wf-controls-styles":{overview:`<p>The seven kit families are a verbatim copy of the ASP.NET-oriented kit in <code>docs/StyleSheets/</code>, so some selectors assume markup that the adapters do not (and plain-HTML users may not) produce. Four sheets are added on top (not kit files): <code>md-</code> (Modal), <code>rp-</code> (Repeater), <code>dl-</code> (DataList) and <code>gv-&lt;t&gt;-edit.css</code> (GridView edit and insert rows). Load <code>&lt;theme&gt;-full.css</code> to get kit plus all of them; <code>&lt;theme&gt;-all.css</code> is the kit alone.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Issue</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>limitation</td><td><strong>Nested pager table.</strong> The kit's GridView pager selectors assume <code>tr.pager &gt; td &gt; table</code>. The adapters emit a flat <code>tr.pager &gt; td</code> with links and spans, so any rule written for <code>.pager table</code> does not apply. The basic <code>.pager a</code> / <code>.pager span</code> rules do. The current page is <code>span[aria-current=page]</code>, and a disabled Previous/Next is <code>span.aspNetDisabled</code>; <code>adapters.css</code> keeps the disabled one from looking like the current page.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><strong><code>.ajax__tab_hover</code> is never toggled.</strong> The tab sheets style a hover state through that class; the adapters rely on <code>:hover</code> only, so the class-based hover rule never fires.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><strong>Menu-style tab variant not emitted.</strong> The kit has a second tab layout (<code>ul.static</code> menu plus <code>.tb-&lt;theme&gt;-panel</code>); <code>WebFormsTabs</code> / <code>wf-tabs</code> emit only the AjaxControlToolkit <code>ajax__tab_*</code> structure, with the header as a <code>ul</code> instead of the toolkit's <code>div</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><strong>Validation highlighting needs ASP.NET globals.</strong> <code>validation-input-highlight.js</code> hooks <code>ValidatorUpdateDisplay</code> / <code>Page_Validators</code>, which only exist on real ASP.NET pages. In plain HTML, React and Angular, toggle the <code>is-invalid</code> class on the inputs yourself from the validators' results. The <code>vl-</code> message and summary classes work without it.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><strong>TreeView layout.</strong> The kit expects nested tables and uses <code>:has()</code> (Chrome and Edge 105+, Firefox 121+, Safari 15.4+). The adapters emit <code>ul</code>/<code>li</code> with <code>div[role=group]</code> children, so <code>adapters.css</code> (loaded after the theme) is needed to remove bullets and style the toggle button. Node <code>+</code> / <code>-</code> glyphs are text buttons, not the kit's <code>img</code> elements.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><strong>Menu flyouts.</strong> The kit only sets appearance; showing, hiding and positioning <code>ul.dynamic</code> is the adapter's job (and yours in plain HTML). The adapters also keep their Bootstrap utility classes (<code>navbar</code>, <code>nav-link</code>, <code>dropdown-menu</code>, ...), which are harmless without Bootstrap.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><strong>Breadcrumb separator.</strong> The glyph is drawn by CSS on <code>.sep</code> (the element is empty, with the text in <code>data-separator</code>), so without the kit or your own <code>.sep::before</code> rule no separator is visible.</td></tr><tr><td>limitation</td><td><strong>No theme for</strong> Calendar, Accordion and AdRotator. The Login family and validators have kit classes (<code>lg-</code>, <code>vl-</code>) but no React/Angular adapter, so you add the class to your own markup. Modal, Repeater, DataList and grid edit rows are covered by the added families (<code>md-</code>, <code>rp-</code>, <code>dl-</code>, <code>gv-&lt;t&gt;-edit.css</code>).</td></tr><tr><td>fixed</td><td>The kit styled only <code>text</code> and <code>date</code> inputs inside a GridView <code>tr.edit</code> / <code>tr.footer</code>, so <code>select</code>, <code>textarea</code>, number / email inputs, checkboxes and buttons in an edit template were unstyled. <code>gv-&lt;t&gt;-edit.css</code> (in <code>&lt;theme&gt;-full.css</code>) now styles them, and an <code>input</code> with no <code>type</code> is handled too.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><strong>Edit templates need controls the families style.</strong> Inside <code>tr.edit</code> / <code>tr.footer</code>, <code>.wf-item.edit</code> and the DataList edit item the sheets style <code>input</code> (text, password, email, number, date and untyped), <code>select</code>, <code>textarea</code>, checkbox, <code>label</code> and <code>button</code>. Other widgets (custom components, <code>input type=range</code>, <code>file</code>, ...) keep browser defaults. Load <code>-full.css</code>: with <code>-all.css</code> only text and date inputs are themed in grid edit rows and Repeater / DataList are unstyled.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td><strong>Backdrop colour.</strong> The modal overlay's colour is <code>var(--wf-backdrop, rgba(0,0,0,.5))</code>; override it with the CSS variable (on <code>:root</code> or the dialog class), not by editing the sheet.</td></tr><tr><td>gotcha</td><td>Theme switching works by changing the class on each control root (<code>gv-modern</code> to <code>gv-dark</code>); changing only the <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> is not enough unless the class suffix matches the loaded theme. Several themes can be loaded at once because every rule is class-scoped.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<hr>
`},"issues-how-to-read-this-page":{overview:'<ul><li>Prefer the numbered table in <a href="#/api/guides/issues-needs-your-attention-first/overview/1-needs-your-attention-first">section 1</a> when deciding whether to adopt a control.</li><li>Every statement was observed in the source and, where it could run in Node, confirmed by executing it. Browser-only code paths (<code>DOMParser</code>, <code>window.location</code>, <code>sessionStorage</code>) are described from the source.</li><li>If you fix one of these, delete its row here and add a regression test in <code>packages/*/test</code>.</li></ul>'}};export{e as default};
